      "summary": "Journey lines can share a name (two \"Prepare an invoice\", two \"Record a receipt\" on P-0101). The link text is identical and only the state tag tells them apart, so a screen-reader link list is ambiguous. Consider an aria-label or visually hidden suffix of \"line text, state\". Not caused by the contract, since the tag is in the same link.",
